 mom tells  him that she's sure  his father is praying for reiner's  success she has no idea that reiner went  to see his dad  and his hopes got completely trampled on  and so the manga is even sadder for  these reasons  but anyways we jump to the island and  the brainwashed and naive  reiner keeps on getting more and more  disillusioned he realizes that he's the  only one present who truly views the  islanders  as pure devils and so felt no remorse at  the thought of destroying them  mercilessly  for him he is like a chosen angel of god  who's charged with fighting pure evil  devils while the others know that  they're going to be killing humans  and the only difference between these  humans is what side of the wall they  happen to be on  then marcel drops the truth bomb and he  says sorry again to reiner suggesting  that he was probably apologizing to  reiner about this the whole time  reiner was never meant to be chosen as a  warrior he was the weakest  however marcel talked down about his  brother and elevated reiner to the  military  so that he could save porco his little  brother from the tragic fate  of becoming a titan shifter and getting  only 13 years longer to live  and even that is only if he didn't die  on a dangerous mission first  this continues to mess with reiner  because his brainwashed self  never thought that being chosen as a  warrior could be a bad thing  so he thinks it's absurd that marcel is  apologizing for making reiner's dreams  come true  reiner's naive ideology was challenged  when he found  out that his father would never accept  him and his mom and now again  when the value of becoming a warrior has  been brought into doubt  in a short period of time everything he  thought he knew  his whole world view and purpose for  living has been brought into serious  doubt  combine all that with being a double  agent child soldier  later on and you can totally see how he  developed mental issues  like split personality disorder but as  if him hearing this truth bomb from  marcel  after everything wasn't traumatizing  enough this is when amir's mindless  titan appears and almost eats reiner  he then witnesses marcel save him and  die before his eyes and then reiner just  runs away  definitely not the behavior you'd expect  from a self-proclaimed hero  at this point reiner is the epitome of  cowardice which you can't really blame  that much because he's a little kid  he's crying thinking that annie and  bertolt got killed  too and that he'll be next when annie  kicks him he screams like a baby  scared out of his mind and it's funny  how annie mentions that reiner for the  first time  beat her in a long distance race which  further emphasizes how scared he was  annie points out that they should have  transformed and stole the jaw titan back  immediately  but when reiner and bethod started  running away so did she  without marcel they have no leader and  that could lead to many more  mistakes and problems as a result annie  wants to go back to marley but  reiner won't have it notably in the  manga he gets a flashback of his mom  saying  she knows he'll be able to complete the  mission and that is why he refuses to go  back now  he doesn't want to disappoint her more  than anything in the anime  annie just suggests that reiner won't go  back because he'll get killed for  messing up  he goes on to rationally explain that  they'll all be in trouble  since they all ran away and catching the  draw won't  be possible because it is the fastest  and can run away and they'll be sitting  ducks after using too much power  annie starts to accept that reiner is  right about them needing to get the  founding titan  but she's also angry and blames him for  the situation  she proceeds to beat him up badly in the  manga it seemed to pass quicker since it  only lasted  a page and a half but in the anime it  affected me more because of how long it  seemed to go on for  reiner then proceeds to tackle annie  holds her in a chokehold and says that  reiner is dead he'll become marcel the  confident leader they need  and that is the moment that reiner  changed from the worst student and  crybaby to the outwardly confident  reiner we see  during the beginning of attack on titan  the one aaron looks up to  obviously reiner is messed up and does  horrible things but i do like this idea  of being able to transform yourself  in order to achieve your goal it's  unfortunate though that reiner's goal  includes making the lives of the aldians  within the walls a living hell  we then come full circle to the  beginning of attack on titan when the  colossal titan appears  except this time we focus on the warrior  perspective in the manga  it did include annie's titan being used  to attract  pure titans so that there would be  maximum destruction after the gate was  destroyed  in the anime they missed this so that  you could potentially assume that annie  didn't have as important a role to play  in the destruction  we also see the smiling titan pass right  by bertolt very abnormal behavior so  this suggests that dina fritz's titan  did appear to be drawn to her husband  grisha yeager and his new family  after all after passing by bertholdt it  can't be a coincidence that she goes for  and kills her old husband's new wife  then reiner transforms  and says he's not ready for this to end  because he still doesn't understand  anything and as  he thinks that he breaks through the  second gate in his armor titan form  notably in the manga the translation is  i don't want this to end here i haven't  changed  anything yet a significantly different  translation so the anime focuses on more  knowledge  while in the manga the focus is on  making an impact on the world before he  goes but either way it's a powerful  moment coming from someone who wasn't  supposed to be born  since marleans aren't supposed to have  kids with aldians he wasn't supposed to  be a warrior and  he was supposed to have died instead of  marcel yet despite all those things he's  still here and refuses to go down  without a fight  without trying to move forward and get  some answers for his seemingly  unwanted existence by the time annie  awakens within wall rose  reiner is the clear leader of the group  comforting them  and saying he'll be the warrior he  should have been keep in mind that  reiner's like a 12 year old child right  now  and he's taking all of this  responsibility on his shoulders although  we know his actions are wrong  we can also see from this episode how he  got to the messed up place he got to  and he clearly wasn't motivated by evil  we also have some fill in the blank  moments in this episode  like how they got their backstory from a  guy who left his children behind when  the titans arrived  and then later hanged himself and we see  annie trail kenny ackerman  trying to find out about the royal  family only to run away from him when  she figures out how skilled he is i  gotta say annie's kick that helps her  get away  is beautifully animated here and despite  some people not loving the cgi  this season i think the animation has  been great so far  if it continues to keep up this level of  animation until the end  i'll be more than satisfied then we get  annie saying to reiner and bertott that  she wants to leave to go back to marley  bring the info they have while reiner  refuses since they have very little  information  considering they've been here for five  years reiner suggests destroying wall  rose  and when annie mentions his new friends  dying reiner says that they are not  friends but devils and despite what  reiner says  it's clear that the lying takes a toll  on him as we'll see later in the episode  when he almost takes his own life annie  is distant and aloof with the others not  wanting to be friends with her enemies  while reiner is even more committed to  killing them but acts like they're best  friends  it's almost scary how good reiner is at  deception though  it does come back to haunt him later on  we see aaron getting tired from training  and reiner showing up like a big brother  to motivate him he asks how he can be  like  reiner and he's worried about dying  without doing a damn thing keep in mind  that's what reiner feared when he broke  through the gate in the manga  dying without doing or changing anything  so the parallel between them  is even more clear in the manga reiner  sees his younger self in  aaron and tells him to do what he has to  do  and to keep moving forward he says  that's all we can do  and finishes off the speech by saying  that he knows aaron can do it and that  behavior  juxtapose with the fact that he's the  enemy who killed aaron's mom and so many  others  is too much for reiner to take it haunts  him to the present day  the lie he lived and we see him in the  present with a rifle in his mouth  the only thing that keeps him from  taking his own life is the fact that  falco happens to hit the wall  and disjogs reiner out of his mental  health and reminds him that he still has  a purpose  to look after the younger generation of  warrior candidates if it wasn't for them  reiner would have already taken his own  life because of all the horrible things  he's done  this episode ends with falco seeing a  self-proclaimed  liar who says he's being treated for  emotional trauma and honestly i feel  like almost everyone in this series  should be treated for emotional trauma  this whole conversation is fascinating  falco is sad because gabby will inherit  the titan power but the wounded  aldian soldier is glad falco won't  inherit the power  because he seems like a good guy and he  wants falco to live a long life but  falco doesn't want gabby to get the  power in his place  because he wants her to live a long and  happy life so he hates the fact that  he's so powerless to do anything about  it  the wounded soldier muses about war and  how if everyone knew what would come of  it nobody would go to war  and i'll quote him here because it's  important stuff he continues and i quote  most people are pushed by something  forced to march into hell  that something wasn't their choice their  situation or others made them do it  but people who push their own backs see  a different kind of hell they can  see something beyond the hell it might  be hope it might be another hell  only those who keep moving forward will  ever know end quote  and bam we see a future aaron looking  back at us  and if you didn't recognize that from  his look and from his overall importance  in the scene  then you'll remember that reiner had  told him the exact same thing in the  flashback about moving forward what a  crazy episode and really served as a  tribute to reiner's character  and his evolution from the beginning to  now how he went from a young optimistic  boy to a suicidal depressed adult  after experiencing the realities of war  first hand and just as reiner decided to  keep moving forward all those years ago  when he broke through the second gate  aaron clearly has a plan to keep moving  forward  putting himself through hell out of his  own free will hoping for something good  but knowing that it may just be another  hell but still he doesn't want to die  without doing anything  i gotta say this is arguably my favorite  manga ever  and the way it captures the complexities  of reality is something very few stories  can do so well  i think this final anime season is going  to be great just as the first three  episodes have been  even though they do cut out more manga  stuff than i would have liked them to  cut out i'm not a huge fan of that  but what can you do either way i am  hyped about this final season i'm hyped  to see how this mind-blowing modern  classic will end  and i can't wait for the next episode  but anyways thanks for watching  if you do want to see episode reviews  like this one for future episodes then  let me know in the comments and by  warhammer  smashing that like button if